#: ../../../reuse/usb-using-rufus.txt:54
msgid ""
"![Rufus finished writing the ISO](/images/rufus/rufus-finished-writing.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/usb-using-rufus.txt:54
msgid "Rufus finished writing the ISO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/create-a-bootable-usb-stick.md:247
msgid "On macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/create-a-bootable-usb-stick.md:249
msgid ""
"On macOS, you have to install a third-party application for writing images "
"to USB sticks. Alternatively, you can use the built-in `dd` tool on the "
"command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/create-a-bootable-usb-stick.md:251
msgid ""
"The USB stick will work on **PC (Windows) hardware** and older Apple "
"hardware based on **Intel CPUs**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/apple-silicon-disclaimer.txt:2
msgid ""
"If you want to run Ubuntu on **Apple Silicon** hardware, such as recent Macs "
"using M1 CPUs or later, refer instead to the [Ubuntu Asahi](https://"
"ubuntuasahi.org/) community project, which isn't supported by Canonical. The "
"hardware support might be limited and depends on your specific machine. For "
"example, Ubuntu Asahi 25.10 only runs on systems with M1 and M2 CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reuse/apple-silicon-disclaimer.txt:4
msgid ""
"You can also install Ubuntu in a virtual machine on top of your current "
"system using [Multipass](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/multipass/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/create-a-bootable-usb-stick.md:256
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"Unfortunately, Disk Utility doesn't seem to be able to write arbitrary "
"images, only macOS disk images. Saving for future reference and "
"reevaluation.\n"
"\n"
"### Using the Disk Utility\n"
"\n"
"The Disk Utility is preinstalled on macOS and you can use it to write any "
"image to your USB stick.\n"
"\n"
"1. Launch the *Disk Utility* app from {menuselection}`Applications -> "
"Utilities` or from the Spotlight search.\n"
"\n"
"1. Insert your USB stick. It appears in the sidebar. Select it there.\n"
"\n"
"    You might need to enable the {menuselection}`View -> Show All Devices` "
"option.\n"
"\n"
"    :::{warning}\n"
"    Make sure to select the USB stick and **not** your internal macOS disk. "
"Both are listed.\n"
"    :::\n"
"\n"
"1. To ensure compatibility with Apple hardware, reformat the USB stick with "
"the GUID partition table:\n"
"\n"
"    Select {guilabel}`Erase` from the toolbar.\n"
"\n"
"    Set the format to *MS-DOS (FAT)* and the scheme to *GUID Partition "
"Map*.\n"
"\n"
"    Check that you've chosen the correct device and click {guilabel}"
"`Erase`.\n"
"\n"
"1. Click {guilabel}`Restore` ({guilabel}`↺`) in the toolbar.\n"
"\n"
"1. Click {guilabel}`Image…` and select the Ubuntu image file.\n"
"\n"
"1. Click {guilabel}`Restore`.\n"
"\n"
"1. Wait for the writing to finish.\n"
"\n"
"1. After the write process has completed, macOS might inform you that \"The "
"disk you inserted was not readable by this computer\".\n"
"\n"
"    Select {guilabel}`Eject` and remove the USB device. Don't select "
"{guilabel}`Initialize`.\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

